NAME
       dnf - install, update and remove software packages

SYNOPSIS
       dnf [OPTION...] COMMAND [ARGUMENT...]

DESCRIPTION
       dnf manages RPM packages on RHEL. It downloads packages from the
       repositories it knows, works out what else they need (dependencies),
       checks their signatures and installs everything together. yum is
       another name for dnf on RHEL 9.

       Commands that change the system need root. dnf shows what it is going
       to do and asks "Is this ok [y/N]:" before it does it; -y answers yes.

   Repositories
       Each repository is a section in a .repo file in /etc/yum.repos.d/:

           [BaseOS]
           name=RHEL 9 BaseOS
           baseurl=http://repo.lab.example.com/BaseOS
           enabled=1
           gpgcheck=1
           gpgkey=file:///etc/pki/rpm-gpg/RPM-GPG-KEY-redhat-release

       baseurl may also be file:///mnt/BaseOS for a mounted DVD. gpgcheck=1
       makes dnf check each package's signature against gpgkey (or a key
       imported with rpm --import); gpgcheck=0 skips the check. dnf
       config-manager --add-repo URL writes such a file for you, but without
       gpgkey.

COMMANDS
       install PACKAGE...
              Install packages, by name, by a file they provide (dnf install
              /usr/bin/dig) or from a local .rpm file.

       remove PACKAGE...
              Remove packages (and packages that need them).

       reinstall PACKAGE...
              Install the same version again.

       upgrade [PACKAGE...], update
              Upgrade the named packages, or all of them.

       check-update
              List the packages that have an update. Exit status 100 means
              updates are available.

       list [installed|available|updates] [PATTERN]
              List packages.

       info PACKAGE
              Show a package's version, size, repository and description.

       search WORD
              Look for WORD in package names and summaries.

       provides FILE, whatprovides FILE
              Which package contains this file (wildcards such as */semanage
              work).

       repolist [--all|--disabled]
              List the enabled repositories (or all, or the disabled ones).

       repoquery [OPTION] PACKAGE
              Ask about packages without installing them, for example
              --requires or -l (the files in the package).

       group list, group info GROUP, group install GROUP
              Work with package groups, such as "Server with GUI" or
              "Development Tools".

       module list, module enable, module install
              Work with module streams (different versions of software such
              as php:8.1) from AppStream.

       history [list|info N|undo N]
              Show past transactions, or undo one.

       clean all
              Remove cached repository data.

       makecache
              Download repository data now.

       autoremove
              Remove packages that were installed only as dependencies and
              are no longer needed.

       config-manager --add-repo URL
              Write a .repo file for URL. --enable REPO and --disable REPO
              switch repositories on or off.

OPTIONS
       -y, --assumeyes
              Answer yes to every question.

       --assumeno
              Answer no: shows what would be done.

       -q, --quiet
              Print less.

       --nogpgcheck
              Do not check signatures for this command.

       --enablerepo=REPO, --disablerepo=REPO
              Use (or leave out) a repository for this command only.

       --repo=REPO
              Use only this repository.

       --refresh
              Treat the cached repository data as out of date.

       -C, --cacheonly
              Use only the cached data.

       --allowerasing
              Allow removing installed packages to solve conflicts.

EXAMPLES
       Use the lab repositories:

           dnf config-manager --add-repo http://repo.lab.example.com/BaseOS
           dnf config-manager --add-repo http://repo.lab.example.com/AppStream
           dnf repolist

       Install the web server without being asked:

           dnf install -y httpd

       Which package has the semanage command?

           dnf provides '*/semanage'

       Install a package from a downloaded file:

           dnf install /root/mypkg-1.0-1.el9.x86_64.rpm

       Use the DVD as a repository:

           mount /dev/sr0 /mnt
           dnf config-manager --add-repo file:///mnt/BaseOS

FILES
       /etc/dnf/dnf.conf
              Main settings (gpgcheck default, installonly_limit...).

       /etc/yum.repos.d/*.repo
              Repository definitions.

       /var/log/dnf.log
              What dnf did.

NOTES
       "Error: GPG check FAILED" or a question about importing a key means
       the repository's key is not trusted yet: add the gpgkey= line, import
       the key with rpm --import, or set gpgcheck=0 when the task says so.

SEE ALSO
       rpm(8), yum.conf(5), dnf.conf(5)
